* Code reuse in\nAztec contracts
** Why no inheritance
*** Noir: structs, traits, generics,\nno "is", no super
*** The aztec macro reads one\ncontract block, one file
*** Composition, not extension
** The contract module owns
*** Entry points + attributes\n(external, authorize_once, only_self)
*** storage struct = slot layout
*** event types (global selector registry)
*** enqueue_self / internal / emit
** Library crates
*** type = "lib", by path or git tag
*** Module structs implement\nStateVariable<N, Context>
*** impl per context: public vs private
*** State variables are values:\npass them as arguments
** Traits instead of virtual
*** Screening trait: what a variant decides
*** One impl per variant\n(FreezeAndLists, FreezeOnly)
*** Generic chain, monomorphised:\nno dispatch, no cost
*** contract_library_method\nfor helpers returning state
** Cost check
*** Calls inlined like internal helpers
*** aztec profile gates before/after:\nidentical circuits
** Contract crates as dependencies
*** Interface only: Token::at(addr)
*** Not the code, not the notes
*** Event selector collision -> stub crate
*** Nested workspace: build from a copy
** What stays per contract
*** Declarations, attributes,\nenqueues, events (~40%)
*** Events: library returns the values,\ncontract emits and delivers
*** Selector test across variants
*** Noir 1.0+: restrictions may lift;\ncomptime macros possible but fragile
@endmindmap
